10. Open questions
1. Which exact state and service will be the first supported workflow? A real 24-hour demo cannot credibly support “every document” or every government service.
2. Is the initial service income certificate, scholarship, pension restart, or another workflow with a publicly accessible portal and acknowledgement receipt?
3. What is the approved real telephony provider, and what legal/compliance review confirms automated calls and recordings are permitted?
4. What identity-verification model is required before handling sensitive documents?
5. Which document types may be retained, for how long, and under which legal basis?
6. Will the product support Aadhaar-derived information at all? The default recommendation is no storage and no processing beyond strictly necessary, user-controlled portal entry.
7. What is the human-support model when portal automation or eligibility interpretation is uncertain?
8. How will the product handle portal terms of use, rate limits, bot detection, and official authorization?
9. What is the escalation path if an official asks for an unofficial payment or directs the citizen to a middleman?
10. Is a real completed submission with acknowledgement number mandatory for the demo? This PRD assumes yes, but the selected service and portal must be validated immediately.

  
