9. Responsive behaviour
Mobile: 360–599 px
- Default experience; one-column layout.
- Persistent bottom primary action, above browser safe-area controls.
- One decision per viewport. Long summaries use expandable sections.
- Full-screen sheets for submission, payment, and consent confirmation.
- Document capture launches camera directly; no hover interactions.
- Portal automation is represented as a clear status timeline, not a tiny remote-browser view.
Tablet: 600–1023 px
- Two-pane layouts for document review and application details.
- Left pane holds the checklist/timeline; right pane holds active content.
- Confirmation actions remain centrally focused and cannot be hidden in a side panel.
Desktop: 1024 px and above
- Three-region case workspace: navigation, application timeline, contextual detail.
- Operators may see queue and case pane together.
- Citizens see more history and document context, but destructive actions remain in a constrained centered confirmation sheet.
- Never use desktop width to make forms denser than the reading-friendly 640–720 px form column.
10. Accessibility
- All normal text must meet 4.5:1 contrast minimum; large text, icons, and focus indicators meet 3:1 minimum. Critical labels use 4.5:1 regardless of size.
- Every status uses text plus icon and shape—not color alone.
- Minimum interactive target: 48 × 48 px.
- Support browser zoom to 200% without lost content or horizontal scrolling at 320 px width.
- Voice is optional input, never the only input. Every voice action has a text alternative.
- Apply lang="hi" or the appropriate language attribute to Indian-language content so screen readers select the correct pronunciation.
- Focus order follows visual/task order: page title → instructions → form controls → help → primary action. Modal focus is trapped; closing returns focus to the invoking control.
- Keyboard support: Tab/Shift+Tab, Enter/Space for controls, Escape for dismissible sheets, and visible skip-to-content links.
- Use semantic landmarks, native buttons/inputs, labeled fieldsets for consent, aria-current="step" for progress, aria-live="polite" for non-critical updates, and role="alert" for blocking failures.
- Voice waveforms are decorative and aria-hidden; the recording state is exposed as text.
- Document thumbnails include meaningful labels but never expose sensitive numbers in alt text.
- Error summaries link to the invalid field; each field uses aria-describedby for help and error text.
- Motion is limited and respects prefers-reduced-motion; progress should never rely on animation alone.